          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "Does the service cause any pain or discomfort?",
            "dsc": "<p>The monthlies test uses the Tasso device to collect blood. Participants in clinical studies have reported lower levels of pain with the Tasso device compared to collecting blood with a finger stick or standard venipuncture procedure.</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_mKU3mh": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "How does a QuickDraw device work?",
            "dsc": "<p>How does the Tasso device work? The Tasso Button sticks to the skin with a light adhesive. When the button is pressed, a vacuum forms and a lancet pricks the surface of the skin. The vacuum draws blood out of the capillaries and into a compatible container attached to the bottom of the Tasso Button.</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_MTMG8w": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "Is this a needle-free blood collection system?",
            "dsc": "<p>Some people refer to Tasso Devices as a needle-free system since it does not use a hollow venipuncture needle to enter a vein.</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_kDb9pr": {
